#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:96
#: 16669aa2f9cf4befb61791936221d552
msgid "The HEEWING F405 supports up to 9 PWM outputs. M1-M2, M5-M6 and M9 support bi-directional dshot. All outputs support dshot although M3-4 are not recommended for this purpose as they share resources with I2C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:98
#: dd0f14ce9f844f2c9f743927363244f8
msgid "The PWM is in 4 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:100
#: d1edff8859ee48bc9a8c9a8915ec19fd
msgid "PWM 1 and 2 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:101
#: e976b37e9e36415285c8d15ec1afc28c
msgid "PWM 3 and 4 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:102
#: 755655ab37c94957a16457e54f8ad8e3
msgid "PWM 5 and 6 in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:103
#: dbc4cbd00c0b4d9081ada471eb6939ec
msgid "PWM 7-9 in group4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:105
#: bf605c9fa9704e639761fb8371b9fc2f
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:108
#: 473b34a886374840958bbe4677fcd3d0
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:110
#: 3b87e5c832fa46c6b75a70af4cf972d8
msgid "The RCIN pin, is passed by an inverter to RX2 (UART2 RX), which by default is mapped to a timer input instead of the UART, and can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 which require a true UART connection. However, FPort, when connected in this manner, can provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:112
#: e75ab72024194ca8953413a2d1b06305
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, the RX2 pin can also be configured to be used as true UART2 RX pin for use with bi-directional systems by setting the :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` to “1” so it becomes the SERIAL2 port's RX input pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:114
#: 8d29ffffa55a48768bf00114604ee08a
msgid "With this option, :ref:`SERIAL6_PROTOCOL<SERIAL6_PROTOCOL>` must be set to \"23\", and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:116
#: 3b40800088ab4280840916feaea773fb
msgid "PPM/SBUS is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:118
#: 9f8697da71c54ca4aa79810ca5b04454
msgid "FPort requires connection to TX2 and RX2 via a bi-directional inverter. See :ref:`common-FPort-receivers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:120
#: 3aa2c4f6e52a4f18adc0a979a5b7ffb7
msgid "CRSF also requires a TX2 connection, in addition to RX2, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:122
#: 7f35d502d84645e1aba5bfad2db41ac0
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to TX2 and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:124
#: 29d451a300d849ea9094c8e8f97b8785
msgid "UART2 is configured by default for serial receivers. You can also have more than one receiver in the system at a time (usually used for long range hand-offs to a remote TX). See :ref:`common-multiple-rx` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:126
#: 77b258835d52459fa0798dd84eff8481
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM (SBUS requires external inversion on other UARTs). See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:129
#: 2cefaa75c1194e4ebc576dc552e5232d
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:131
#: 9d922276ab454b8d8eb85af0059832d1
msgid "The HEEWINGF405 supports using its internal OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver). External OSD support such as DJI or DisplayPort is supported using any free UART. See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2` for more info."
msgstr ""

